WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.480
Having trouble keeping track of Spider-Man's
big-screen adventures?

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.360
With a cinematic legacy spanning nearly 20
years, multiple directors, and numerous actors,

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.220
we don't blame you.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.959
So to help out, we'll break down all the events
of Tom Holland's appearances as your Friendly

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.340
Neighborhood Spider-Man, step-by-step.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.160
What the F-?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.160
Surprisingly, Peter Parker's first appearance
in the MCU doesn't come in Captain America:

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:30.660
Civil War.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.600
Instead, that honor goes to Iron Man 2, where
Tony Stark saves a little kid during the climax

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.260
of the film.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.460
While Tony's flying in to stop Ivan Vanko
from using weaponized Hammer drones to attack

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.350
the attendants at the Stark Expo, a young
boy in an Iron Man mask raises his toy gauntlet

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.710
to stop one of the drones.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.420
Iron Man swoops in, blasts the robot, and
tells his pint-sized fan…

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:55.540
"Nice work, kid."

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.160
… before blasting off again.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:03.300
Fans have long speculated that the masked
child was actually a young Peter Parker, years

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.500
before Marvel got the go-ahead from Sony to
officially add Spider-Man to the MCU.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.140
After all, the Stark Expo takes place in Queens,
and Peter is a long-time science geek who

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.680
wouldn't miss the opportunity to go to an
event like that.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.979
Tom Holland told The Huffington Post in 2017
that as far as he and MCU head honcho Kevin

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.620
Feige are concerned, that unnamed boy is definitely
Peter Parker.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:28.100
The actor even, quote, "triple-confirmed"
it, so it's about as canonical as one can

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.100
possibly be.

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:34.539
By the time Spider-Man: Homecoming hit theaters,
audiences had seen Peter's Uncle Ben die on

00:01:34.539 --> 00:01:39.450
the big screen twice in two different franchises,
so it's no wonder that the filmmakers of Spider-Man:

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.220
Homecoming chose to skip over that particular
part of Spider-Man's origin story.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:48.100
That said, there's been enough hints and references
to make it clear that the MCU version of Peter

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.740
definitely had an Uncle Ben that he lost at
some point.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:56.300
In Spider-Man: Far From Home, Peter's luggage
looks second-hand and bears the initials "BFP."

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.600
The luggage almost certainly belonged to one
Benjamin Franklin Parker before Peter used

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.100
it.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.580
According to Spider-Man: Homecoming writers
Jonathan Goldstein and John Francis Daley,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.890
an earlier draft of the film would have seen
Aunt May explicitly mention her dearly departed

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:10.380
husband.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.500
With all that, we can peg Uncle Ben's death
at around six months before the events of

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.500
Captain America: Civil War, since that film
shows Peter telling Tony that he's had his

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.040
powers for "six months."

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.560
Peter even indirectly mentions that he blames
himself for Uncle Ben's so-far mysterious

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.760
death by saying that,

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:34.440
"When you can do the things I can, but you
don't, and then the bad things happen, they

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.200
happen because of you."

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.260
In other words …

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.640
"With great power comes great responsibility."

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.440
Six months after Peter gets his powers, Tony
drops by Aunt May's apartment to sample some

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:50.940
of her walnut date loaf and meet the mysterious,
arachnid-themed superhero who's been showing

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.680
up on YouTube.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.280
Peter explains what he's all about as a young
superhero, and Iron Man adds him to his team

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:00.189
of Avenger-hunting Avengers, as part of his
ongoing feud to take down Bucky.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.939
So Peter heads to Berlin, does some sightseeing,
and annoys Tony Stark's bodyguard and pal,

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:05.440
Happy Hogan.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.940
"shush"

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.219
Then he gets a costume upgrade courtesy of
Tony Stark, and fights against Captain America,

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.440
Winter Soldier, Falcon, Ant-Man, Scarlet Witch,
and Hawkeye.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.180
Spider-Man acquits himself nicely in the fight
until the whole melee ends with Tony's best

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.120
friend, Rhodey, wounded by friendly fire.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.140
As for Peter, he suffers a pretty frightening
fall, although he ultimately emerges unscathed

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.140
unlike Rhodey.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.480
The whole experience seems to put Tony off
of the idea of using literal teenagers to

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.100
help him catch a brainwashed former KGB assassin,
which is probably for the best.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.640
However, Peter seems to have had a good time,
as he filmed pretty much the entire battle.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.180
After the harrowing events of Captain America:
Civil War, Peter heads back to Queens with

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.560
his new, more technologically advanced Spider-suit.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.040
Tony tells Peter that the Avengers will "let
him know" if there are any future missions,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.600
and in the meantime, he should go to school
and focus on being a local hero.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.560
Two months later, while swinging around on
his after-school crime-fighting rounds, he

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:12.100
interrupts an ATM heist organized by crooks
who are using high-tech and extremely dangerous

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:12.600
weapons.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.740
Peter eventually follows up on the weapons
dealers and gets into a fight with their leader,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:17.240
the Vulture.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:21.940
Tony sends a drone to bail Peter out and give
him yet another talking to about how Peter

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.940
should stop trying to fight supervillains.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.880
"Can't you just be a…

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.500
Friendly…

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.740
Neighborhood Spider-Man?"

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.670
"But I'm ready for more than that now!"

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:32.940
"No, you're not!"

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:37.340
Peter half-listens mostly to the parts about
how his suit has a ton of capabilities that

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.480
he didn't know about and gets his buddy Ned
to hack the suit and give him full access.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.500
Round two with the Vulture in Washington,
D.C. ends with Peter trapped in a warehouse

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.500
for the night, and when he heads off for round
three on a ferry ride in New York, it turns

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.850
out that Iron Man and the FBI had organized
a sting operation that Peter inadvertently

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:54.800
interrupts.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.260
Disappointed in his protégé, Tony takes
back the suit, and Peter recommits to his

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:02.120
regular life and asks his crush, Liz, to prom.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:07.020
Unfortunately, Liz's dad is the Vulture, forcing
Peter to take him down in his original low-tech

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.800
suit before the winged villain can steal a
ton of valuable Stark tech.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:16.220
Spider-Man succeeds, Vulture goes to prison,
Liz moves to Oregon with her mom, and Tony

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:19.060
offers Peter a place on the Avengers roster
if he wants.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.680
Instead, Peter turns him down, choosing to
focus on being a friendly neighborhood Spider-Man

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.180
for a while.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.960
"Last chance: Yes or no."

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.460
"No."

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:26.960
"OK.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.660
That's kind of a Springsteen-y, working class
hero vibe that I dig."

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.940
When Thanos and his Black Order invade Earth
in search of the ultra-powerful Infinity Stones

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:40.510
in Avengers: Infinity War, Spider-Man hops
right in to help Iron Man, Dr. Strange, Bruce

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:42.000
Banner, and Wong in defending Earth.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:47.160
Dr. Strange is kidnapped by the Black Order's
Ebony Maw, and Peter chases after him, hitching

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.920
a ride on Maw's spaceship before it flies
away completely.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.460
Tony quickly joins him, giving the younger
hero the even more high-tech super suit last

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:58.020
seen at the end of Homecoming to help him
battle Thanos' crew of aliens.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:03.300
Spidey and Iron Man free Dr. Strange, blast
Ebony Maw out into space, and land on Titan,

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.530
Thanos' home planet.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:09.180
They're quickly joined by some of the Guardians
of the Galaxy: Peter Quill, Drax, Mantis,

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:09.720
and Nebula.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:10.880
“Woah woah woah woah!

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.000
Please don’t put your eggs in me!”

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:18.240
The heroes prep to fight Thanos, who soon
arrives to take Dr. Strange's Time Stone to

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.560
add to his Infinity Gauntlet.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:24.520
The heroes put up a valiant effort, but their
plan goes south, and Thanos teleports to Earth

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.040
after nabbing the Time Stone.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.880
Soon after, he gets the Mind Stone from Vision,
puts it all together, and snaps his fingers,

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.380
causing half of all life in the universe to
fade away.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:38.460
Unfortunately, Peter's 50/50 probability comes
out on the negative side, and he turns to

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.560
dust in Tony's arms on an alien planet.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:42.740
"I'm sorry."

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.840
After Thanos kills off half of the universe,
the remaining half is left to mourn their

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.000
fallen friends and family.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.980
Unfortunately for Peter, it doesn't seem like
there are many left to remember him.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:02.460
Virtually all of his friends along with Aunt
May are "blipped" by Thanos after the Mad

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.390
Titan snaps his big purple fingers.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.800
For the five years between Thor killing Thanos
in the beginning of Avengers: Endgame and

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:13.060
when Captain America gets the gang back together,
it seems like the only one left to mourn Peter

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.060
is Tony Stark.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:17.780
He even keeps a framed picture of his young
protégé in the kitchen of his cabin home.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:22.500
Luckily for Spider-Man, Tony eventually feels
guilty enough to rejoin the Avengers.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.360
Once he's back on the team, he develops a
time travel machine, goes back in time to

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:30.440
steal the Infinity Stones before Thanos could
destroy them in the present timeline, and

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.420
reconstructs another Infinity Gauntlet.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.060
And with one snap of Hulk's mighty hand, the
dusted half of the universe is restored exactly

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.580
how they were when they disappeared.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:43.100
Thanos from a previous timeline heads to the
present in order to re-snap everything into

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:49.030
oblivion, but every superhero or superhero-adjacent
character stands in his way including Spider-Man.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:50.220
“What are you doing?”

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:56.920
“Oh this is nice.”

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:01.680
Peter joins the fight, meets some of his new
superhero peers, murders a bunch of aliens

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:06.140
with his suit's "Instant Kill Mode," and then
watches as Tony Stark gives his life to dust

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.000
Thanos' crew with a snap of his own.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.420
After all that space alien craziness, it's
back to normality for everyone's favorite

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:18.030
wall-crawler in Spider-Man: Far From Home
well, until he finds himself suddenly embroiled

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:22.380
in a fight against multiversal Elementals
alongside a superhero from another universe:

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.520
Quentin Beck, aka Mysterio.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:29.240
To make things worse, Peter's struggling to
live up to Iron Man's legacy — and to control

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.140
a high-tech, sunglasses-based AI system called
EDITH.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.380
Plus, his feelings for MJ are coming to a
head.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.400
Puberty, man!

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.020
"You look… really pretty."

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.420
"And therefore I have value?"

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.360
"No — no, that's not what I meant at all.

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:41.860
I was just — "

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:42.860
"I'm messing with you."

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:47.140
Desperate for a mentor, Peter gives up the
sunglasses to Beck, whose magic powers and

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:51.060
big brother attitude seem to make him a better
successor to Tony than Peter could ever hope

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:51.560
to be.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:56.180
Unfortunately, Beck's running a con on Peter,
as he's amassed a villainous group of former

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:00.140
Stark Industries employees to help him trick
the world into thinking he's the next Iron

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:00.640
Man.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:04.960
Peter learns the truth and eventually defeats
Mysterio, with the villain seemingly dying

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:05.980
in the final battle.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:10.260
Spidey returns to New York having saved the
day, and everything seems to be going well.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:16.280
Until, that is, J. Jonah Jameson of TheDailyBugle.net
leaks Mysterio's dying confession and reveals

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.260
to the entire world that Peter Parker is Spider-Man.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.620
So we’re all set up for a nice, neat follow-up
to that cliffhanger, right?

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:28.140
Welp, after Sony and Disney failed to extend
their Spider-man agreement in August 2019,

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.260
the entire Spidey future is up in the air.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.600
Does Sony continue where Far From Home left
off?

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.020
Do they cash in on the meme and go with a
Spider-Man: Homeless theme?

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:41.500
The possibilites are endless, and also unpredictible
- nobody’s spidey-sense is tingling just

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:42.000
yet.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.720
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.100
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.740
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

